			"notes": "# Panorama Mod\n### Version 1.1.0\n\nTurn your favorite Minecraft views into a custom main-menu background.\n\nPanorama Mod lets you capture a panorama from inside your world, manage your saved captures, and export them as resource packs—all without leaving Minecraft.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Capture panoramas:** Name your capture and take all six panorama images.\n- **Browse your collection:** View previews of your saved panoramas.\n- **Manage captures:** Rename or delete them from the built-in browser.\n- **Export resource packs:** Create a ready-to-use ZIP for your title-screen background.\n- **Open your capture folder:** Access your saved files directly from the mod.\n\n## How to use\n\n1. Find a spot in your world that you want to capture.\n2. Press **F6**, enter a name, and start the capture.\n3. Open **Panoramas** from the title screen, or press **F7** to open the settings menu.\n4. Select your capture and choose **Export**.\n5. Enable the exported pack in Minecraft’s **Resource Packs** menu.\n\nBoth keybinds can be changed in **Options → Controls**.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Fabric Loader\n- Fabric API\n\nThis is a **client-side mod**. Servers do not need to install it.\n\n## Feedback\n\nFound a bug or have a suggestion? Open an issue on [Discord](https://discord.com/invite/KjNUUDfaJN)."
		},
